OL,2,V55555555CBANK FAILS TO HALT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSTERLING'S SLIDE
OL,5, The Bank of England bought pounds to
OL,6, shore up sterling but it failed to halt
OL,7, a slide, prompted by fears over the
OL,8, Government's poor ratings in the polls.
OL,10, After an early rally it dipped more
OL,11, than a cent against the dollar and four
OL,12, pfennigs against the West German mark.
OL,14, Fears that inflation could hit 9% have
OL,15, raised the possibility of another rise
OL,16, in interest rates, even though they are
OL,17, failing to dampen demand for credit.
OL,19, Credit card companies and other lenders
OL,20, advanced #3.95bn in January compared to
OL,21, #3.38bn in December, denting Chancellor
OL,22, John Major's hopes of curbing borrowing
OL,23,F]DFrom 05-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
